\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every $\eta\in(0,1)$, is there a compact $E\subset[0,1]$ of Lebesgue measure greater than $1-\eta$ containing no set
\[
\{a+b2^{-n}:n\geq1\}
\]
for real $a$ and nonzero real $b$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every $\eta\in(0,1)$, does some compact $E\subset[0,1]$ of Lebesgue measure greater than $1-\eta$ avoid containing $\{a+b2^{-n}:n\geq1\}$ for every real $a$ and every nonzero real $b$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-dyadic-case-of-the-Erdos-similarity-conjecture-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

